        "original_id": "340cd5d3-74f3-5121-a1f4-c96bde1635ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Iowa, University of Texas at Austin, Butler University, University of Michigan, Ball State University\n- Places: Iowa City, Iowa, Austin, Texas, Texas State Capitol, Chicago\n- People: David Loughery, Dave Allerdice\n- Programs: Iowa Playwrights Workshop\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Iowa was founded in 1847 and is the oldest university in the state of Iowa.\n- The University of Texas at Austin was founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas.\"\n- Dave Allerdice played football for the University of Michigan from 1907 to 1909.\n- Dave Allerdice coached football at Butler University in 1910.\n- Dave Allerdice coached football at the University of Texas at Austin from 1911 to 1915.\n- The University of Iowa is a flagship public research university in Iowa City, Iowa, and is also known as the UI, U of I, UIowa, or simply Iowa.\n- The University of Iowa is organized into eleven colleges that offer more than 200 areas of study and seven professional degrees.\n- The campus of the University of Texas at Austin is in Austin, Texas, about 1 mile from the Texas State Capitol.\n- David Loughery was born in Chicago.\n- David Loughery attended Ball State University and the University of Iowa.\n- David Loughery was a member of the Iowa Playwrights Workshop at the University of Iowa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
