        "text": "Page: University of Iowa. Sentence: The University of Iowa (also known as the UI, U of I, UIowa, or simply Iowa) is a flagship public research university in Iowa City, Iowa.\nPage: University of Iowa. Sentence: Founded in 1847, it is the oldest university in the state.\nPage: University of Iowa. Sentence: University of Iowa is organized into eleven colleges offering more than 200 areas of study and seven professional degrees.\nPage: University of Texas at Austin. Sentence: Founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas,\" its campus is located in Austin, Texas, approximately 1 mile (1.6 km) from the Texas State Capitol.\nPage: David Loughery. Sentence: Born in Chicago, Loughery attended Ball State University and the University of Iowa where he was a member of the Iowa Playwrights Workshop.\nPage: Dave Allerdice. Sentence: He played football for the University of Michigan from 1907 to 1909 and coached football at Butler University (1910) and the University of Texas at Austin (1911–1915).",
